From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 10:48:09 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: Draw and track another process's menu through a copy
 kept up to date.

A process may call on another's menus now, and a window takes such a menu
for its menu bar, as Word's document window does with the shared menu
Excel builds while a worksheet is active in place.  Laying that bar out,
drawing it and tracking it, as tracking a popup of another process, needs
the items here, and nothing showed.

A menu of another process that this one shows is now shown through a
copy made here: its items as they are over there, with the handles of
their submenus as they are, so that the application still hears of the
menus it knows (WM_INITMENU, WM_INITMENUPOPUP, WM_MENUSELECT,
WM_MENUCOMMAND, WM_MENUCHAR, GetMenuBarInfo, MN_GETHMENU).  The copy is
made when the menu becomes a window's menu or is first shown, brought up
to date when the menu bar is laid out or DrawMenuBar is called and once
the application has been told a menu is about to show, and goes when the
menu does.

With this Word shows Excel's menu groups in its menu bar while the
worksheet is active in place, and makes room for them, which is what
tells Excel where its toolbars go.  The test checks that a window takes
another process's menu for its menu bar as on Windows, where
tools/menuprobe in the outer tree measured it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 7886337ea24d3084bbb709f2a16b44c82e4dd846)

